  "question": {
    "text": "A complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> is said to be unimodular if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are complex numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>z</mi></menclose><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is unimodular and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is not unimodular, then the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> lies on a&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "circle of radius <math> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "straight line parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "straight line parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
